# The arena's one foliage type: the bushes standing on the slope between the walls and the first
# hills. The mesh reference names bush.obj's Bush sub-asset — three quads crossed at sixty degrees,
# carrying the whole of leaves-albedo.png each — and the instances live in Outskirts.vxfol beside
# this file, generated by TerrainSeed and committed for the same reason the terrain is.
#
# ⚠ **The silhouette is the map's alpha, not the mesh.** `Foliage.rvn` alpha-tests against
# `alphaCutoff`, so the card cross reads as a leaf cluster; without the test it is three
# intersecting slabs of the colour the authoring tool left under the transparent margin. This is the
# content that makes that test observable, which is why the stand exists at all.
#
# ⚠ **One albedo for the whole palette, so this palette has one type.** `FoliageDrawPass.Albedo` is
# a single `Texture2D` binding and `TerrainSceneRenderer.AlbedoOf` resolves the first type in the
# palette that names one — so a second type here would draw through the bushes' leaves map whatever
# it named. That is what keeps `bark` unseated: a trunk needs a texture per type, and the shape that
# would give it one is recorded on `FoliageDrawPass.Albedo`.
name: Bush
mesh: vx:9a745bce11d8456db1f67ba97a59b796#b5761ecb
albedo: vx:b52ac26f9cda4406b1c667297a987cbd
storage: Stored
radius: 1.2
minScale: 0.8
maxScale: 1.6
startCullDistance: 70
endCullDistance: 90
castShadows: true
# FoliageEcology.None spelled out: a zeroed ecology fails its own validation (maxAge 0 is a species
# that never grows), which would refuse the whole volume at extraction.
ecology:
  shadeTolerance: 1
  maxAge: 1
